/* ===================== v0.26.7: live player count (behind the scenes) =====================
   Every copy sends an anonymous heartbeat: one "+1" on a public counter for the current 2-minute window
   (abacus.jasoncameron.dev, free, no account). Nothing about the player or the save is sent - no name, id,
   seed or version; the URL only holds the window number. Only a copy with the dev flag (a file named
   dev-playercount.txt in the app's userData folder) reads the count back and shows "Live player count: N"
   small on the pause screen. Live = copies that checked in during the last full window (2-4 min).
   Fails silently offline: every request is fire-and-forget with a 6s timeout, nothing waits on it.
   v0.26.19: 15s timeout (the counter service can take 10s+), the last good count is kept in localStorage
   (burrow_pc_n) and shown right away at startup and through failed reads, and a failed read retries after 20s. */
